<title>GREECE: GREEK VEPAL CHANGES NAME TO ELVAL.</title>
<headline>GREEK VEPAL CHANGES NAME TO ELVAL.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Athens bourse's main market metallurgical firm Vepal changed its name to ELVAL effective today, the bourse said in a statement.</p>
<p>Vepal shares will be replaced with 0.408133443 new shares of Elval, it said.</p>
<p>The opening price was 2,430 drachmas per share and there has been no trade so far in the session. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
